Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:45:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] bus: brcmstb_gisb: Get the breakpoint interrupt as
 optional

The breakpoint interrupt is optional: the probe only requests it when
bp_irq > 0, and SoCs whose GISB arbiter has none (such as the BCM7231)
probe fine without it. But it is fetched with platform_get_irq(), which
logs an error when the interrupt is absent:

  brcm-gisb-arb 10400000.gisb-arb: error -ENXIO: IRQ index 2 not found

Use platform_get_irq_optional(), which returns the same value without
logging.

Fixes: fb8a0b80c4bb ("bus: brcmstb_gisb: Add support for breakpoint interrupts")
---
 drivers/bus/brcmstb_gisb.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/brcmstb_gisb.c b/drivers/bus/brcmstb_gisb.c
index 91ef99c..e0135e0 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/brcmstb_gisb.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/brcmstb_gisb.c
@@ -420,7 +420,7 @@ static int __init brcmstb_gisb_arb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	timeout_irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
 	tea_irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 1);
-	bp_irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 2);
+	bp_irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 2);
 
 	gdev = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*gdev), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!gdev)
